From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: v0lumehi <aljic.zijad@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 21:21:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Textures: decode BC6H into RGB9E5 on GPUs without BC support
 (DM_BC6H_RGB9E5)

On an iPhone or iPad before the A17 Pro the GPU does not read BC textures, so a profile with tex_bc_cpu
decodes them on the CPU. BC6H (HDR) went to RGBA16Float, 8 bytes a pixel, and a scene with many of them can
pass the process's memory limit. DM_BC6H_RGB9E5=1 decodes BC6H into RGB9E5Float, 4 bytes a pixel: half the
memory, with negative values clamped to 0 and a 9-bit mantissa. It is off by default so the tested decode
stays, and only takes effect when g_bc_cpu is on. The shader chain is untouched.

nvn_bcdec.c: nvn_bc_set_bc6h_rgb9e5 / nvn_bc_bc6h_rgb9e5 choose what nvn_bc_unpacked answers for 0x4f / 0x50,
nvn_rgb9e5_pack is the reference shared-exponent packing, the block decode packs each half-float pixel.
nvn_mtl.m reads the switch where g_bc_cpu is set. The upload path already sizes its staging from the
unpacked bytes per pixel. settings.tsv has a Performance row for iOS games with tex_bc_cpu, docs/settings.md
and docs/env_switches.tsv describe it. The iOS shell hides the row on a GPU with BC support.

Tests: t_bcdec.c (the packing against an independent decode, the format map with the switch on and off, the
RGB9E5 pixels equal the RGBA16F pixels packed, edge blocks) and test_launcher_settings.py (who sees the row).

Upstream-Status: fork-only (declined seedds/nxnative#488)
Reason: HDR textures on a phone without BC support can pass the memory limit, a front end needs a switch for the smaller format
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#544
